# The Ghost original signs off with an explicit line break
# ('Sincerely, <br />' then the team name); Medium's importer turned it
# into the same doubled break it uses for wrapped source lines, which
# convert collapses to a space for Ghost-migrated posts. Make it a
# single break in every Medium-side copy (export, the page's rendered
# DOM, and the page's stored paragraph text) so the signature keeps its
# own line whichever body source converts.
file: b79bfd18566d/export.html
old: Sincerely,<br><br>
new: Sincerely,<br>

file: b79bfd18566d/page.html
old: Sincerely,<br/><br/>
new: Sincerely,<br/>
old: "text":"Sincerely,\n\nThe JupyterHub Team
new: "text":"Sincerely,\nThe JupyterHub Team
